  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5703.10 Procedure for Any Person or Any Public or Private Agency to Request and Receive a Copy of the Criminal Conviction Record of Another.\n\n(a) To obtain a criminal conviction record of another, the requestor shall present a completed criminal conviction record release authorization form to the central repository, as specified in Saf-C 5703.11, in person or by mail.\n\n(b) The criminal conviction record release authorization form utilized shall be as follows:\n\nTable 5700-1 Criminal History Record Information Release Authorization Forms\n\nForm Number | Title | How to Obtain:\n\nDSSP 256 | Criminal History Record Information Request Form (eff. 7/15/16) | www.nh.gov/safety/nhsp Department of Safety Division of State Police – Criminal Records Unit (603) 223-3867 33 Hazen Drive Concord, NH 03305\n\nDSSP 371 | DHHS/DCYF Relative Criminal Check Only (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 372 | License Exempt Child Care Form NH RSA 170-E:3-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of Operations Support – Child Care Licensing Unit (603) 271-9025 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 373 | Applicants to Practice Medicine NH RSA 329:11-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-4728, 121 South Fruit Street, Suite 301, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 374 | Applicants to Physician Assistants RSA 328-d:3-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-4728, 121 South Fruit Street, Suite 301, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 375 | BDS Area Agencies or Community Mental Health Centers (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division of Community Based Care Services – Bureau of Behavioral Health (603) 271-5007 105 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 376 | TANF Requests for Child Care Form NH RSA 170-E:7, II (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division of Family Assistance – Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (603) 271-9700 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 377 | New Applicant – Adoptive Parents Form NH RSA 170-B:18 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 378 | Background Check Request of Alcohol and Other Drug Use Counselors NH RSA 330-C (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-6761, 121 South Fruit Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 380 | Driver Education Instructors NH RSA 263:44-b, II (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/safety/dmv Department of Safety Division of Motor Vehicles – Driver Education (603) 227-4075 23 Hazen Drive Concord, NH 03305\n\nDSSP 381 | Child Day Care NH RSA 170-E:7, II – Child Care Institutions RSA 170-E:29-a:II (eff. 02/20/15) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of Operations Support – Child Care Licensing Unit (603) 271-9025 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nForm Number | Title | How to Obtain:\n\nDSSP 382 | School Employee/Volunteer Criminal History Record Check RSA 189:13-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/safety/nhsp Department of Safety Division of State Police – Criminal Records Unit (603) 223-3867 33 Hazen Drive Concord, NH 03305\n\nDSSP 383 | County Employee Criminal History Background Check NH RSA 28:10-c (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/government/local Counties Select Specific County\n\nDSSP 384 | DCYF Personnel (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of the Commissioner – Human Resources (603) 271-9344 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 385 | DHHS Area Agencies (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division of Community Based Care Services – Bureau of Developmental Services (603) 271-5133, 105 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 386 | Department of Safety Employees NH RSA 21-P:15-c (7/15/16) | www.nh.gov/government/state Department of Safety Division of Administration (603) 223-8000 33 Hazen Drive Concord, NH 03305\n\nDSSP 387 | Board of Nursing NH RSA 326-b:15 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-2323, 121 South Fruit Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 388 | Renewal – Foster Parents Form NH RSA 170-E:29 (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 389 | New Applicant – Foster Parents Form NH RSA 170-E:29 (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 390 | Hawkers, Peddlers, and Vendors Background Checks RSA 31:102-a & b (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/government/local Select Specific Municipality\n\nDSSP 391 | Municipal Employee/Volunteer Candidate Background Checks NH RSA 41:9-b (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/government/local Select Specific Municipality\n\nDSSP 392 | Licensing of Game Operators NH RSA 287-D:12 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.racing.nh.gov (603)271-3391 14 Integra Drive, Concord, NH 03301\n\nForm Number | Title | How to Obtain:\n\nDSSP 393 | Real Estate Appraisers Board NH RSA 310-B:6-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Technical Professions (603) 271-2219, 121 South Fruit Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 394 | Serve America Act Employees or Volunteers (eff. 10/1/16) | Provided to Applicant by Specific Employer\n\nDSSP 406 | Renewal – Adoptive Parents Form NH RSA 170-E:29 (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 407 | Child Day Care RSA 170-E:7, II–Child Care Institutions RSA 170-E:29-a, II (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of Operations Support – Child Care Licensing Unit (603) 271-9025 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 408 | Consumer Reporting Agency (eff. 7/15/16) | Provided to Applicant by Specific Employer\n\nDSSP 409 | DCYF Intern/Volunteer Criminal Check Only (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 410 | DHHS-DCYF Behavioral Health Provider (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division of Community Based Care Services – Bureau of Behavioral Health (603) 271-5007 105 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 411 | DHHS Bureau of Behavioral Health (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division of Community Based Care Services – Bureau of Behavioral Health (603) 271-5007 105 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 412 | Applicants for Initial Registration/Reinstatement as A Medical Technician RSA 328-I:7 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-8389, 121 South Fruit Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 413 | PL 108-79 Federal Prison Rape Elimination Act (PREA) [Contractor] (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 414 | PL 108-79 Federal Prison Rape Elimination Act (PREA) [Staff] (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 415 | Therapeutic Cannabis Program RSA 126-X:4, 8 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of Operations Support – Therapeutic Cannabis Program (603) 271-9234 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 416 | DHHS/DCYF Transportation and Child In Home Care (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Child Development (603) 271-4242, 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 417 | New Hampshire Medicaid Program (eff. 10/1/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Office of Improvement and Integrity – Program Integrity Unit (603) 271-4344 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nForm Number | Title | How to Obtain:\n\nDSSP 419 | NH Banking Department/Banking Division (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh,gov/banking (603) 271-3561 53 Regional Drive, Suite 200, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 420 | Nursing Home Administrators NH RSA 151-A:6-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.oplc.nh.gov Office of Professional Licensure and Certification – Division of Health Professionals (603) 271-4728, 121 South Fruit Street, Suite 301, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 421 | Emergency Medical and Trauma Services NH RSA 153-A:10-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh.gov/safety/fstems/ems Department of Safety Division of Fire Standards and Training- Bureau of Emergency Medical Services (603) 223-4200 98 Smokey Bear Blvd Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 422 | NH Department of Revenue Employee Candidate Background Checks RSA 21-J:3-a (eff. 10/1/16) | www.revenue.nh.gov (603) 230-5000 109 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 424 | New Hampshire Banking Department/Consumer Credit (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh,gov/banking (603) 271-8675 53 Regional Drive, Suite 200, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 425 | Games of Chance Facility License NH RSA 287-D:8, VII (eff. 10/1/16) | www.racing.nh.gov (603)271-3391 14 Integra Drive, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 426 | NH Banking Department Employees RSA 383:7 (eff. 10/1/16) | www.nh,gov/banking (603) 271-3561 53 Regional Drive, Suite 200, Concord, NH 03301\n\nDSSP 427 | Foster/Adoptive Adult Household Member Form NH RSA 170-E:29 (eff. 7/15/16) | www.dhhs.nh.gov Divisions/Offices; Division for Children, Youth and Families – Foster Care and Adoption (603) 271-4440 129 Pleasant Street, Concord, NH 03301\n\n(c) In addition to the criminal conviction record release authorization form, $25.00 shall be included for the record check.\n\n(d) On receipt of a completed criminal conviction record release authorization form and $25.00, a copy of the requested criminal conviction record shall be given or sent to the requestor.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5700) #6704, eff 3-3-98; amd by #8173, eff 9-21-04; amd by #8591, INTERIM, eff 3-24-06, EXPIRES: 9-20-06; ss by #8651, eff 6-2-06; ss by #9329, eff 11-21-08, EXPIRED: 11-21-16\n\nNew. #12132, eff 3-17-17",
